  m_text: 'A probe''s picture is taken from one point. Without Box Projection, every surface reads it as if the surroundings were infinitely far, so its reflection slides when the camera moves. With Box Projection, the picture is fitted to the probe''s box, and the reflections stay in place inside it.


    <b>Predict:</b> You move the camera sideways along the arcade. With Box Projection off, what does the glow''s reflection on the floor do?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Move this camera sideways and watch the floor.

    2. Tick Box Projection on the Reflection Probe.

    3. Move the camera again.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Reference 17</color></size>'
