  m_text: 'A planar reflection is a second camera, mirrored below a flat floor, that renders the scene again every frame. The floor''s shader shows that picture. It is sharp, complete and in the right place, but only for one flat plane, and it costs a second render of the scene.


    <b>Predict:</b> The Planar Reflection component mirrors this camera at Plane Height 0. You raise the floor to 0.5 m and leave Plane Height at 0. What happens to the reflections?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Select Reflection Camera (a child of Planar Reflection) and find it in the Scene view.

    2. Raise the Floor to Y 0.5.

    3. Set Plane Height to 0.5; then set both back to 0.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: the toolbox''s Reflections showcase</color></size>'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -6055507529455485361, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
